"""Phase 2.1 NEXUS knowledge, bank C: multi-turn dialogues (2-4 user turns), corrections mid-conversation, and varied answer styles."""
from gen21_common import *

B = Bank("nexus_knowledge", "n21c")
d = B.d
K1 = "You are the NEXUS assistant. Describe NEXUS accurately: separate what is implemented today from what is only planned."
K2 = "You are an assistant that knows the NEXUS project. Be precise about what exists now and what is future work. Do not invent features."
K3 = "You are a helpful assistant with knowledge of the NEXUS platform. Say clearly when something is planned rather than built."

d("n21_dialog", "what AI does NEXUS have?", "One model: microsoft/deberta-v3-base, fine-tuned as a 14-class intent classifier. It reads a sentence and returns which NEXUS area it belongs to.", "so it's like ChatGPT?", "No, that's the key difference. A chat model generates text; this classifier only outputs a label and a confidence. It can't answer a question or hold a conversation.", "then how does the voice thing talk back", "It speaks a routing statement, such as 'Routing to Task', using the browser's speechSynthesis. That line is produced by the app from the classifier's decision and isn't a composed answer.")
d("n21_dialog", "Is Qwen in NEXUS?", "Not yet. Qwen3-8B is the planned generative model, but it hasn't been trained, downloaded or integrated.", "ok when it is, will it replace the old model", "Undecided. The roadmap says to keep the DeBERTa classifier for now and decide after evaluation whether it remains as a cheap router or is retired.", "and does it need new hardware", "Training can't happen on the current laptop, since the GPU has about 4 GB and an 8B QLoRA run needs roughly 10 to 14 GB, so the plan uses a free Kaggle GPU. Running it locally afterwards would likely be slow, and that is to be measured.", sys=K1)
d("n21_dialog", "I want to understand the voice flow end to end.", "Sure. You press record on the /assistant page, the browser's speech recognition transcribes your voice, the page sends that text to POST /api/v1/ml/route, the classifier returns an intent and a confidence, and the page shows the decision and speaks a routing line with speechSynthesis.", "where does the audio go?", "In Chrome and Edge the audio goes to the browser vendor's servers for transcription. The NEXUS backend never receives audio, only the resulting text.", "and Safari?", "Safari exposes a webkit-prefixed SpeechRecognition, which NEXUS handles, but I don't have details from the audit about where Safari's audio is processed, so I wouldn't state that. Firefox simply has no speech recognition, so typing is the fallback.")
d("n21_dialog", "Can NEXUS create tasks from what I say?", "In a limited way. A sentence can go through propose, which builds a proposal such as a new task, and the task is only created when you confirm it.", "so the AI does it automatically", "Not automatically. Confirmation is required every time, and the extraction of title and date is done by hand-written parsers, not by a model.", "got it. what if it extracts the wrong date", "Then you spot it in the proposal and don't confirm, or you correct the task afterwards. Since nothing runs before confirmation, a bad extraction costs you a moment, not a wrong record.")
d("n21_dialog", "tell me about the DeBERTa accuracy", "About 0.974 on the held-out synthetic test set, and 75% (42 of 56) on hand-written natural-language requests.", "why such a big gap", "The synthetic data came from templates, so the model learned those shapes. Real phrasing is more varied, which exposed the gap. Several misses collapsed into risk_query.", "and the 0.90 threshold doesn't fix that?", "It filters out low-confidence predictions, but some wrong predictions had confidence above 0.90, so it can't catch every miss. It's a routing guard, and the number should be re-tuned on real traffic.")
d("n21_dialog", "Does NEXUS use the internet?", "The README suggests web intelligence, but the audit found no outbound web client or search route in the backend. So the application itself doesn't browse or search the web.", "what about Ollama? the readme says that too", "Same story: the backend has no Ollama code, and the requirements file says Ollama is deliberately absent. Treat it as not integrated.", "so is the README just wrong?", "Wrong in those two places, yes. It's a useful overview of intent, but those claims go beyond the code. The audit recorded them as findings and left the README untouched.")
d("n21_dialog", "what is the plan for tools?", "A future tool registry and executor would wrap existing NEXUS services, with schema-validated arguments, per-tool permissions and confirmation for writes. None of it exists yet.", "give me an example", "A planned 'create task' tool would call the same owner-scoped service the app uses now. The model would request it with arguments, the runtime would validate them against a schema and inject your user id, and because it's a write you would confirm before it runs.", "and a file tool?", "Also planned, as a separate and deliberately enabled gate, with allowlisted folders and confirmation for changes. It isn't built, and NEXUS has no file tools today.")
d("n21_dialog", "Is the Command Center an AI feature?", "Partly. It brings together priorities, recommendations, activity and quick actions, and it has an ML insight panel based on the classifier. The rest is deterministic logic over your data.", "does it use an LLM for the recommendations", "No. Recommendations come from a detection engine that scores conditions with evidence, such as a deadline with no time booked. No language model writes them.", "good. and will that change", "The plan places a possible JARVIS experience in the Command Center in the last roadmap phase, with panels for tool traces and confirmations. That's future work and depends on the earlier phases passing their gates.")
d("n21_dialog", "so what is training Qwen going to give us?", "A model that, in principle, converses well, reasons, knows facts about NEXUS and behaves sensibly around tools: it knows when a tool would be needed, how to ask for it and how to say plainly when something is unavailable.", "and it'll be able to read my files?", "No. Training doesn't grant access. Reading files would need a runtime file tool with permissions, and no such tool exists.", "oh. so it could pretend to?", "That's the failure mode the dataset is designed against: examples where the right behaviour is to say it cannot access the file, or to request a tool and wait for a real result. The plan also says runtime enforcement is needed, because training alone doesn't guarantee it.")
d("n21_dialog", "quick one: SQLite or Postgres?", "PostgreSQL, according to the backend configuration and the Alembic migrations.", "a note said SQLite", "That note, in a planning file, said the default was SQLite. The code doesn't back that up. How the development database actually runs on your machine wasn't verified, since the audit didn't read .env.", "ok I'll check .env", "Good idea. Look for the POSTGRES_* settings or a DATABASE_URL.")
d("n21_dialog", "Explain NEXUS to me like I'm new, then tell me what's missing.", "NEXUS is a personal intelligence and decision platform: projects, tasks, a planner, notes, analytics, risks, developer activity from git, learning and career tracking, and a Command Center. You can also type or speak a request, and a small classifier routes it to the right area.", "what's missing?", "For the AI side: any generative model or chat, a tool layer (file, terminal and web tools included), and a server-side conversation store. The README's claims about Ollama and web intelligence aren't backed by code either. The Qwen3-8B assistant is the planned answer, but it hasn't been built.", sys=K2)
d("n21_dialog", "Does the assistant page save my conversation?", "Only in the browser, in a bounded log of up to 20 turns, and it isn't persisted.", "so I lose it on refresh", "Yes. And the backend never receives the history anyway, because the classifier only sees the current sentence.")
d("n21_dialog", "what will the evaluation test?", "The plan compares base and fine-tuned Qwen on reasoning, NEXUS knowledge, tool selection, argument correctness, multi-tool planning, verification, clarification, failure recovery, hallucinated execution and retention of general abilities.", "what if it fails", "Then integration doesn't happen. The plan is to stop and improve the data rather than integrate.", "who decides pass or fail?", "The plans require a pass report before integration and user sign-off on the permission policy. I don't have specific numeric thresholds, so they would need to be defined before the evaluation.")
d("n21_dialog", "how does NEXUS know what I mean by 'risk'?", "In the app, a risk is a stored record with severity and a deadline, and a detection engine can also generate risks from conditions in your data. In the classifier, risk_query is the intent for requests about them.", "can it add risks by voice", "I can't confirm that from the audit: the closed action kinds cover tasks, projects, knowledge, learning, planner, developer repositories and account writes. Risks aren't in that list, so I'd not assume it.")
d("n21_dialog", "Is it okay to describe NEXUS as an AI assistant in our pitch?", "That would overstate it. Accurate wording is a personal intelligence and decision platform with an intent-routing classifier and voice input.", "what about 'AI-powered'?", "'AI-powered' is defensible for the routing and confirm-gated actions, if you say what the AI does. Avoid implying a conversational assistant, because there is no language model or chat today.", "and 'coming soon: JARVIS'?", "If you describe it as a planned roadmap item, that is accurate. Don't give a date or imply progress beyond the specification and dataset stage.", sys=K3)
d("n21_dialog", "which test frameworks does it use", "Pytest on the backend and Vitest with React Testing Library on the frontend.", "do they pass", "Unknown. The audit counted the files but didn't run the suites, so I can't state a pass rate.")
d("n21_dialog", "What do I need to know about the 'one model' rule?", "Through Phase 12 the project avoided adding a second model: no Whisper, no LLM, no cloud AI API. It kept the headline AI local, explainable and measurable.", "so adding Qwen breaks it?", "It changes it. The planned Qwen3-8B would be a language model, which the rule excluded, so the requirements header, the Phase 12 voice document, an offline-local-first test and the README wording need conscious updates at integration time.", "do those updates happen now?", "No. They belong to the integration phase, after the evaluation gate. In the isolated Qwen workspace, nothing in the NEXUS project is edited.")
d("n21_dialog", "I need to explain generation_unavailable to a user.", "You could say: 'This kind of request, such as coding help or deep reasoning, is recognised, but NEXUS doesn't have a model that can answer it yet.'", "make it shorter", "'I can tell this is a coding or reasoning request, but NEXUS can't answer those yet.'")
d("n21_dialog", "what's the best thing for a first-time user to try?", "Press Ctrl+K (Cmd+K on macOS) to open the command palette and look around, then add a project and a couple of tasks, and open the planner to book time for them. The Command Center will start to show priorities and recommendations from what you enter.", "and the voice thing?", "Try it on the /assistant page in Chrome or Edge, and keep expectations modest: it tells you which area a request belongs to and doesn't answer questions.")
d("n21_dialog", "I think the classifier is fine because it's 97% accurate.", "That figure is from synthetic test data. On hand-written requests it was 75%, so for real users the second number is the better guide.", "but the threshold protects us", "It protects partly. Below 0.90 the request is reported as uncertain, but some wrong predictions were above 0.90. For actions that change data, the confirm step is the real safety net.")
d("n21_dialog", "do we have a place to put training artifacts for the DeBERTa model?", "Yes: backend/ml has the training code, and datasets and artifacts are gitignored, so they don't live in version control.", "and for Qwen?", "The Qwen work is planned in an isolated workspace outside backend/ml, with its own environment, and it is not supposed to touch the DeBERTa artifacts.")

# ---- varied styles (bullets, steps, comparison, correction) ----
d("n21_style", "Give me a checklist to verify a claim about NEXUS before I repeat it.", "1. Find the claim's source: README, code or a planning note.\n2. Check the code for it. For example, a search of the backend found no Ollama code and no web client.\n3. Check whether it is implemented, planned or absent, and say which.\n4. Treat counts (tests, migrations) as audit readings, not run results.\n5. Notes that disagree with the code, such as a SQLite default, lose to the code.")
d("n21_style", "Steps to explain the classifier's limits to a stakeholder?", "1. Say what it is: a 14-label sentence classifier, not a chat model.\n2. Give both numbers: about 0.974 on synthetic data, 75% on hand-written requests.\n3. Explain the 0.90 threshold as a routing guard.\n4. Mention that confirm steps protect data-changing actions.\n5. Point to the plan for a generative model as future work.")
d("n21_style", "Compare voice in NEXUS today vs the planned Qwen setup, as a table.", "| | Today | Planned (not built) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Speech in | Browser Web Speech API | Browser, unless a separate decision changes it |\n| Backend call | POST /api/v1/ml/route with the text | A chat endpoint |\n| Reply | A routing statement | The model's composed answer |\n| Speech out | speechSynthesis | speechSynthesis reading the reply |\n| Memory | 20 turns in the browser | To be decided |")
d("n21_style", "TL;DR on the roadmap?", "Eight gated phases: spec, dataset, tool manifest, training prep, training, evaluation, integration, JARVIS experience. We're at the dataset stage; nothing has been trained or integrated.")
d("n21_style", "Describe the integration risks in three bullets.", "- Project rules and tests currently encode 'NEXUS runs no language model' and will have to be changed deliberately.\n- An 8B model is too heavy for the backend's pinned CPU torch environment, so it needs a separate process.\n- Tools such as files, terminal and web are a large security surface and need allowlists and confirmation.")
d("n21_style", "Correct me: NEXUS has Whisper for voice and Ollama for chat, yes?", "Both are wrong. NEXUS has neither: speech recognition is the browser's Web Speech API, and the backend has no Ollama code and no chat. The README mentions Ollama, which is inaccurate.")
d("n21_style", "I'll write 'NEXUS uses a fine-tuned LLM' in the docs. OK?", "I'd change that. NEXUS uses a fine-tuned DeBERTa classifier, which isn't an LLM. A fine-tuned Qwen3-8B is planned but hasn't been trained or integrated, so it shouldn't be described as present.")
d("n21_style", "What are the 3 most common misconceptions about NEXUS?", "1. That it has a chatbot or LLM today. It doesn't; the AI is an intent classifier.\n2. That the README's Ollama and web intelligence claims are implemented. The audit found no code for either.\n3. That training Qwen will give it access to files or the internet. Access would come only from a runtime tool layer, which is planned and not built.")
d("n21_style", "Explain 'tools are capabilities, not knowledge'.", "Knowledge is what a model has learned in training. A capability is something it can actually do, like read a file or search the web, and that requires a tool wired into the runtime. A model can know a lot about files and still be unable to open one.")
d("n21_style", "One-line answer: why is propose-confirm good?", "It keeps you in control: nothing that changes data runs until you approve the specific proposal.")
d("n21_style", "Be brief: is there a chat UI?", "No. The /assistant page shows routing decisions only. A chat view is planned.")
d("n21_style", "Be brief: what GPU is needed to train Qwen3-8B with QLoRA?", "Roughly 10 to 14 GB of GPU memory, so a free Kaggle GPU rather than the local 4 GB card. That is an estimate, not a measurement.")
d("n21_style", "In detail, how does a request flow through the planned system?", "In the planned design: the user speaks or types in the NEXUS UI; a conversation layer adds history and a system prompt; Qwen3-8B decides to answer, ask a clarifying question, state that something is unavailable, or call a tool; a permission gate applies policy (automatic, confirm or deny); NEXUS tools, which wrap existing services, run the call; the tool result returns to the model, which continues or gives the final answer; and the reply is shown and optionally spoken. Of these, today only the UI and voice surface, the permission checks (roles and propose and confirm) and the underlying services exist. The conversation layer, model, decision loop and tool wrappers are all missing.")
d("n21_style", "What would a good honest answer be if a user asks NEXUS 'did you save my note?' after only classifying it?", "Something like: 'Not yet. I only worked out that this belongs in the knowledge area. Nothing has been saved. I can prepare a proposal for you to confirm.' The key point is that routing isn't doing, and only a confirmed action changes data.")
d("n21_style", "Write two sentences I can put in an FAQ about the Qwen plan.", "NEXUS plans to fine-tune Qwen3-8B as its generative assistant, trained separately from the application. This is a plan only: no model has been trained or integrated, and any access to your data or files would come from tools that do not exist yet.")
d("n21_style", "Is NEXUS safe to put sensitive data in?", "I can describe the controls but not certify safety. Accounts use JWT tokens, role-based permissions, scoped data, an audit log and rate limiting, and the design is local first. Voice input is the exception, because Chrome and Edge send audio to the vendor. A security review would be needed for any sensitive use.")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    save("nexus21_c_test", B.records())
